In order to minimize the potential negative impacts of releasing frontier
Pokémon AI models on the broader competitive Pokémon landscape, **pkmn.ai** has
worked with [Smogon](https://smogon.com) and [Pokémon
Showdown](https://pokemonshowdown.com) to produce the following guidelines
related to publishing work product responsibly.

::: aside

Academic papers, technical writeups, game engines, network\ /\ search
infrastructure, human replay\ /\ team databases, and hosted post-game analysis
tools are all broadly considered to be reasonable artifacts to share openly.

Turnkey solutions, model weights, training harnesses, self-play trajectories or
training datasets, live-game analysis tools, and Pokémon Showdown integration
are discouraged --- avoid sharing them outside of trusted collaborators and
researchers.

:::

This policy is expected to change based on how AI and competitive Pokémon evolve
over time. For the time being, you might consider including a line in your
`README.md` as follows:

> Certain aspects of this project have been redacted before release to preserve
> competitive integrity in accordance with the community's [Responsible
> Release](https://pkmn.ai/release) policy.

When redacting your project, please ensure that these artifacts cannot be
recovered from the version control history --- creating a clean repository may
be a safer and easier way to prevent these artifacts from leaking.


If you have any questions about whether what you want to release is considered
safe, please ask in the [chat](https://pkmn.ai/chat) or contact
[pre@pkmn.cc]{.email}.